Here are step-by-step command-line setup guides and configuration templates for both **NixOS System Configuration** and **Home Manager / Homelab Setup**.

---

### Part 1: NixOS System Configuration (`configuration.nix`)

NixOS manages operating system features—such as kernel modules, user accounts, systemd daemons, and system-wide packages—declaratively through `/etc/nixos/configuration.nix`.

#### Step 1: Initial Generation & Editing
When installing NixOS, generate or open your initial configuration file:
```bash
# Generate baseline hardware and configuration files (during installation)
sudo nixos-generate-config --root /mnt

# Edit system configuration
sudo nano /etc/nixos/configuration.nix
```

#### Step 2: Configuration Template (`configuration.nix`)
Below is a standard NixOS system configuration structure:

```nix
{ config, pkgs, ... }:

{
  imports = [
    ./hardware-configuration.nix
  ];

  # Bootloader setup (UEFI example)
  boot.loader.systemd-boot.enable = true;
  boot.loader.efi.canTouchEfiVariables = true;

  # Networking & Hostname
  networking.hostName = "nixos-node";
  networking.networkmanager.enable = true;

  # Time zone and Locale
  time.timeZone = "America/New_York";
  i18n.defaultLocale = "en_US.UTF-8";

  # Global unfree package permission
  nixpkgs.config.allowUnfree = true;

  # Declare User Accounts
  users.users.myuser = {
    isNormalUser = true;
    description = "Primary User";
    extraGroups = [ "networkmanager" "wheel" "docker" ];
  };

  # System-wide packages
  environment.systemPackages = with pkgs; [
    vim
    git
    curl
    wget
    htop
  ];

  # Enable system SSH daemon
  services.openssh.enable = true;

  # Set state version (do not alter after initial install)
  system.stateVersion = "24.11";
}
```

#### Step 3: Command-Line Operations
Apply, test, or roll back system builds using `nixos-rebuild`:

```bash
# Test and activate configuration without setting it as boot default
sudo nixos-rebuild test

# Rebuild system and set as default boot entry
sudo nixos-rebuild switch

# Rebuild from a dotfiles repo in user space
sudo nixos-rebuild switch -I nixos-config=/home/myuser/.dotfiles/nixos/hosts/nixos-node/configuration.nix

# Roll back to the previous working system generation
sudo nixos-rebuild switch --rollback
```

