### Part 2: Home Manager Configuration (`home.nix`)

**Home Manager** declaratively manages user dotfiles, shell environments, and unprivileged user packages without requiring `root` access.

#### Step 1: Embed Home Manager as a Module in NixOS
To manage dotfiles and user configurations atomically during `nixos-rebuild switch`, add the Home Manager module directly into `/etc/nixos/configuration.nix`:

```nix
{ config, pkgs, ... }:

let
  home-manager = builtins.fetchTarball "[suspicious link removed]";
in
{
  imports = [
    ./hardware-configuration.nix
    (import "${home-manager}/nixos")
  ];

  # Recommended Home Manager settings
  home-manager.useGlobalPkgs = true;   # Uses system evaluated pkgs
  home-manager.useUserPackages = true;   # Links user packages to user profiles
  home-manager.backupFileExtension = "backup"; # Backs up conflicting dotfiles

  # Define per-user Home Manager configuration
  home-manager.users.myuser = import ./home.nix;
}
```

#### Step 2: Configuration Template (`home.nix`)
Create `home.nix` in the same directory (or inside `~/.config/home-manager/home.nix` for standalone use):

```nix
{ config, pkgs, ... }:

{
  home.username = "myuser";
  home.homeDirectory = "/home/myuser";

  # Declarative user packages
  home.packages = with pkgs; [
    ripgrep
    fd
    fzf
    btop
    bat
  ];

  # Declarative Git configuration
  programs.git = {
    enable = true;
    userName = "Your Name";
    userEmail = "you@example.com";
  };

  # Shell configuration & aliases
  programs.bash = {
    enable = true;
    enableCompletion = true;
    shellAliases = {
      nrs = "sudo nixos-rebuild switch";
      ll = "ls -la";
    };
  };

  # Manage arbitrary dotfiles via symlinks
  home.file.".config/alacritty/alacritty.toml".text = ''
    [font]
    size = 12.0
  '';

  # Home Manager state version
  home.stateVersion = "24.11";
}
```

#### Step 3: Command-Line Operations
Activate Home Manager updates depending on installation style:

```bash
# If using embedded module inside NixOS
sudo nixos-rebuild switch

# If using standalone Home Manager installation
home-manager switch
```

