### Part 3: Homelab Services Configuration

NixOS allows running server and homelab services (like Docker, Syncthing, reverse proxies, and Pi-hole) directly inside `configuration.nix`:

```nix
{ config, pkgs, ... }:

{
  # 1. Containerization (Docker)
  virtualisation.docker.enable = true;

  # 2. File Synchronization (Syncthing)
  services.syncthing = {
    enable = true;
    user = "myuser";
    dataDir = "/home/myuser/Sync";
    configDir = "/home/myuser/.config/syncthing";
  };

  # 3. Pi-hole / DNS Server
  services.pihole-ftl = {
    enable = true;
    openFirewallDNS = true;
    openFirewallDHCP = true;
  };

  # 4. Firewall Ports Configuration
  networking.firewall = {
    enable = true;
    allowedTCPPorts = [ 80 443 22 8384 ]; # HTTP, HTTPS, SSH, Syncthing Web UI
    allowedUDPPorts = [ 53 21027 ];        # DNS, Syncthing Discovery
  };
}
```

